9: // the transport only when its own down flag is off — the LB consults the
10: // component's isDown() through the network and steps the cursor past a down
11: // seat to the next healthy backend. Each backend stepped over tallies
12: // `skipped` (cumulative; read back via skippedCount() and carried in
13: // snapshot(); lastSkip() names the seat the most recent selection crossed),
14: // while the down address sees a send or a delivery from this selection.
15: //
16: // All-down fail-out: with no healthy candidate the selection is skipped and
17: // the request crosses the transport to the cursor's own seat, so the
